---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="GitHub Actions (CI/CD)">
  <h1>GitHub Actions (CI/CD)</h1>
  <p>
    <code>.github/workflows/deploy.yml</code> is what turns a merged pull request into a live
    site. On every push to <code>main</code> it:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Installs dependencies with <code>npm ci</code></li>
    <li>Runs native Node tests with <code>npm test</code></li>
    <li>Runs <code>npm audit --audit-level=high</code>; high or critical advisories fail the build job</li>
    <li>Builds and uploads the Astro site using the pinned Astro action</li>
    <li>Deploys the built site to GitHub Pages</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    This safe version pins its directly referenced Actions to verified full commit SHAs and gives
    the build read-only repository access. Only the deploy job receives Pages and identity-token
    write permissions. Both Node setup inputs use Node 22.
  </p>
  <p>
    Pull requests and manual workflow dispatches run the build checks but never deploy.
    Deployment requires a push to <code>main</code> and configured Pages permissions.
    Dependency review is not a step in this workflow; required-check enforcement is a separate
    repository setting, not something this file proves.
  </p>
</Layout>
